    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How to express age in German",
     "texto": [
      "In English we say «I am 20 years old», and in German only the verb **sein** (to be) is used:",
      "**Ich bin zwanzig Jahre alt.** (I am twenty years old).",
      "The short form is also completely natural: **Ich bin zwanzig.**",
      "To ask someone's age:",
      "Informal: **Wie alt bist du?** (How old are you?).",
      "Formal: **Wie alt sind Sie?** (how old are you? – formal).",
      "Third person: **Wie alt ist dein Bruder?** (How old is your brother?) → **Er ist fünfzehn.**",
      "Careful! Saying «*Ich habe zwanzig Jahre*» is completely wrong in German: age always goes with **sein**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
